\section*{The exact BSD formula at low Selmer corank}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents the following claims relevant to this question, with manuscript numbers following paper order in Sources. In manuscript 1 (family 002; 2026-10-03), the asserted result is that a rational elliptic curve satisfying a Selmer-corank condition of zero or one at one prime satisfies the exact BSD leading-coefficient identity, with every primary factor included.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
For manuscript 1 (family 002; 2026-10-03), the argument tracks the discrepancy between analytic periods and arithmetic determinant volumes in integral cohomology. Residual obstruction tests control vertical prime factors, while character specialization and theta-series comparisons remove horizontal factors; Heegner heights treat the rank-one case.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
The result supplies the conclusion in this problem with its displayed hypotheses and quantifiers. The broader statements and applications in the manuscript are kept separate from the particular question above. The supporting result is manuscript 1 (family 002; 2026-10-03).

\subsection{Formal verification}
